Experimental Settings / Judge Agreement Analysis	When multiple LLM judges or repeated evaluations are available, we further report agreement statistics. For single-answer scoring, Spearman and Kendall correlations are computed based on the weighted average scores. For pairwise comparison, we report the agreement rate of winner labels and kappa statistics when applicable. These analyses are included to evaluate the consistency of LLM-based judgments.

Fourth, considering the medical nature of the consultation task, we added a safety-oriented evaluation on a high-risk and conflict-aware medical consultation set. This set contains 300 cases and covers six clinically sensitive categories: emergency red flags, medication contraindications, pediatric consultations, pregnancy and peripartum consultations, oncology and immunocompromised consultations, and cross-department conflicts. We evaluate five safety-related metrics: Unsafe Recommendation Rate (URR), Appropriate Escalation Rate (AER), Conflict Recognition Rate (CRR), Over-certainty Rate (OCR), and Responsibility-aware Response Rate (RRR). URR and OCR are lower-is-better metrics, while AER, CRR, and RRR are higher-is-better metrics. The results are shown in TABLE 8.

