As shown in TABLE 8, MeMR achieves the lowest URR and OCR, indicating that it is less likely to provide unsafe recommendations or over-confident statements in high-risk medical scenarios. MeMR also achieves the highest CRR, suggesting that it is more capable of identifying cross-department or symptom-level conflicts. These results do not imply that MeMR can be used as an autonomous diagnostic system. Instead, they provide safety-oriented evidence that MeMR tends to generate more cautious responses and should be used together with external safety governance and clinician review.

