Discussion / Limitation	Although the proposed evaluation protocol and safety-oriented analysis improve the transparency and reliability of the reported results, they do not constitute comprehensive clinical safety validation. MeMR should not be used as an autonomous diagnostic or treatment system. In practical deployment, it should be integrated into a clinician-in-the-loop clinical decision-support workflow with risk detection, uncertainty warning, audit logging, version control, and rollback mechanisms.

Through these revisions, we have improved the reproducibility, transparency, and statistical reliability of the LLM-based evaluation. We have also added safety-oriented analysis for high-risk medical consultation scenarios and clarified that MeMR should be used as an assistant component rather than a replacement for medical professionals.
